        'Resolve each momentum into components with p_x = p cos θ and p_y = p sin θ, measuring θ from the +x axis. Add the x column and the y column separately, then rebuild the total with |p| = √(p_x² + p_y²) and θ = tan⁻¹(p_y/p_x), checking the quadrant.',
        'For a perfectly inelastic 2D collision, the combined object moves along the total momentum vector with speed |p|/(m₁ + m₂). For glancing collisions where objects separate, you usually know some outgoing information and solve for the rest.',
